Subject: [BioC] DESeq2, plotting residuals vs.fitted values
In-Reply-To: <CANkSkzra9QwpYsh=hb7cMPhAaz-3ukasZCiyDRAdotToQ1b4bA@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CANkSkzra9QwpYsh=hb7cMPhAaz-3ukasZCiyDRAdotToQ1b4bA@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <CADqzidWS74NpSYZw_nnb0CtyaWQmqUtS_zrCSsJFcDS=FWGgaw@mail.gmail.com>

On the scale of the counts, the fitted values are: assays(dds)[["mu"]]

to get the fitted values on the common scale, you just need to divide
each column by the size factor:

fitted.common.scale = t( t( assays(dds)[["mu"]] ) / sizeFactors(dds) )

So then the residuals are

counts(dds, normalized=TRUE) - fitted.common.scale



