Dear Quynh,

Since I am also using Mac OS X Lion 10.7.5, here are my steps how to 
compile root:

./configure --help
./configure macosx64 --with-cc=gcc --with-cxx=g++ --with-ld=g++ 
--with-f77="/usr/bin/gfortran-4.2"
make
. bin/thisroot.sh
(Since you have bash there is no need to do "source bin/thisroot.sh")

This setting is for compiling root with gcc.
For clang configure should be:
./configure macosx64 --with-f77="/usr/bin/gfortran-4.2"

The warnings can be ignored.

BTW, I think that the binary 
root_v5.34.05.macosx106-x86_64-gcc-4.2.tar.gz should work on Lion, too.

Best regards,
Christian



